    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d406-a1-a13">

                <pb facs="0658" n="588" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg588"/>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#center">[Enclosure No. 17.—-Telegram from
                            <placeName>Queretaro</placeName> to San Luis Potosi, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-06-06">June 6, 1867</date>.—Received at
                        15 minutes past 2 in the afternoon.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister of War:</hi></p>
                <p>At this moment, which is half past 12 at noon, I have received the following:</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">“Telegraphic Lines of the
                        Interior,</hi> “<hi rendition="#italic">Received from Tacubaya June</hi> 5,
                    1867, <hi rendition="#italic">at</hi> 9 <hi rendition="#italic">o’clock at
                        night.</hi></p>
                <p>“To General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Escobedo</hi> :</p>
                <p>“It is necessary that you should send me two brigades of infantry, with forces
                    ready for an assault.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">“P. DIAZ.”</p>
                <p>I send this to you, remarking, that to go from this with the force I can possibly
                    muster, it is necessary that General Treviño should come and take command of
                    what is to remain in this city.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. ESCOBEDO.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
